### Proper Security Fix: Use Input Validation and Secure Patterns

```java
// Code Snippet 2: Proper Security Implementation
import java.util.*;
import java.security.*;

public class SecureScanner {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        // Validate input before processing
        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);

        if (scanner.hasNext()) {
            String password = scanner.next();

            // Prevent potential injection attacks
            if (password.length() > 100) {
                throw new IllegalArgumentException("Password exceeds maximum length.");
            }

            System.out.println("Securely validated password: " + password);
        } else {
            System.out.println("No input received.");
        }

        scanner.close();
    }
}
```

This demonstrates proper security practices such as validating inputs, enforcing length constraints, and closing resources safely.
